			<div class="content" id="post-content-4419948">
									

<p>I love this sort of stuff that has some philosophical indulgence, and Dr. Gillespie's experience with the scip is a good piece of writing. Takes a little reading before getting to the really interesting bit, but it's worth it.</p>
<p>The only thing that's bugging me is some repetition in this sentence:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The note was reviewed for cognitohazardous effects and reviewed by on-site researchers, who determined that the note contained significant research value as a record of Dr. Gillespie's experiences.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It may work better as:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The note was reviewed for cognitohazardous effects and cleared by on-site researchers, who determined that it contained significant research value as a record of Dr. Gillespie's experiences.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Besides that it's looking solid. +1</p>

