					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606834596" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;" >TheMightyMcB</a></span> <span class="odate time_1573475435 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Nov 2019 12:30</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4420468">
									

<p>I found myself tossing this one back and forth in my head. The read itself was excellent and you really got to show off your prose skills here, so much so that I found myself upvoting by the time I finished.</p>
<p>Then, I went back and reread, and that led to me getting <em>really</em> hung up on that final note from Gillespie. In that sense, I find myself agreeing with Rounderhouse above. The article smacked me in the face with &quot;note at the end syndrome&quot;, to a degree that I honestly have trouble ignoring. It stretched my suspension of disbelief just a tiny bit farther than I was willing to let it go, and that ultimately led me to novoting here, despite my enjoyment of the writing itself.</p>
<p>If I may offer a personal suggestion here, I think an exit interview with Gillespie (perhaps just before his final amnestization?) would be a better way to have this conversation with your readers. It would forego a lot of the (frankly excellent) prose that Gillespie displays in his note, but it would be far more verisimilar. Just food for thought.</p>
<p><span style="font-size:smaller;"><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> <em>Opinions expressed in this review do not reflect the opinions of SCP Wiki staff as a whole. Please respond to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4483018&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573475434" alt="TheMightyMcB" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4483018)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/themightymcb" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4483018); return false;">TheMightyMcB</a></span> or contact the captain of the Site Criticism Team, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1573475434" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;">SoullessSingularity</a></span>, for any questions or concerns relating to this review.</em></span></p>

